cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pwm_dose_equivalence in published research, please cite both the software and the framework paper."
title: "pwm_dose_equivalence: Reference implementation of the signal-equivalence framework for medical-imaging dose-reduction claims"
abstract: >-
  pwm_dose_equivalence is the reference implementation of the
  signal-equivalence framework: a formal, modality-general replacement for
  vendor-style claims like "50 % dose reduction" with a testable 5-tuple
  credential (signal_ratio, task, epsilon, alpha, subpopulation). The
  library exposes a single modality-agnostic API
  (signal_equivalence_credential) that produces a content-addressed
  credential JSON for CT / MRI / PET / user-implemented modalities, plus
  an audit_credential function and pwm-audit CLI for non-coder
  verification of published credentials.
type: software
version: "0.2.2"
